      "file": "emergency_ventilation_fan_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Start on gas, purge fast, never ignite",
      "description": "Emergency ventilation runs at high rate when gas detection reaches its first alarm (often ≈ 10–20 % LEL), diluting a leak below its flammable range and venting it outside. Equipment in the air stream must suit the hazardous-area zone (Ex d / Ex e motor, temperature class) and the impeller–casing pair must be non-sparking (e.g. aluminium/bronze vs steel) — a rub must not cause a spark. The gravity damper closes when the fan stops, keeping weather out. Supplies are typically on essential power.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
